<title>USA: US BANKS FREE RESERVES $528 MLN JULY 30 REVISED TWO WEEKS.</title>
<headline>US BANKS FREE RESERVES $528 MLN JULY 30 REVISED TWO WEEKS.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. commercial banks had revised free reserves of $528 million per day in the two weeks ended July 30, versus revised free reserves of $1.077 billion in the previous two-week period, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>Seasonal borrowings were $363 million versus $299 million a day. Extended credits were nil.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
